# Architecture

The virtual root shares a lockfile and environment across `packages/*` and `apps/*`.
Libraries own regular packages below the PEP 420 namespace `__NAMESPACE__`.
The dependency direction is services → core; applications can depend on either.

See [the ownership ledger](workspace-ledger.toml). Update it when adding a member or
changing allowed internal dependencies; run `uv run inv workspace.check` afterward.
Put dependencies in the importing member, and declare internal workspace sources.
Public import paths are part of the compatibility contract.

Core provides validation and Loguru configuration. Services contains application logic.
Applications own logging initialization; imports never reconfigure global sinks.
Console logging uses the custom formatter; JSON logging preserves structured kwargs.
